962	    /// 61-63 are v1 temporal bits **9-11**, so any v1 edge with
963	    /// `temporal >= 512` reads a NON-ZERO spare. Apply a version gate on
964	    /// edges of unknown provenance — the same rule `truth()` already states
965	    /// for bits 59-60 at its own threshold (`temporal >= 128`).
