1034	    /// Return new edge with the texture-band projection set (bits 61-63).
1035	    ///
1036	    /// Consuming builder, register-style (`edge.with_reasoning_band(b)`),
1037	    /// matching `with_spare`/`with_topology`. Shares storage with
1038	    /// `spare`/`with_spare` — the last writer of either view wins, by
1039	    /// construction, since it is one 3-bit register read through two
1040	    /// lenses. See [`crate::layout::ReasoningBand`] for the full semantics,
1041	    /// # ⚠ Writing a non-zero band perturbs the deprecated `temporal()`
1042	    ///
1043	    /// `temporal()` reads bits **52..63**, a window that CONTAINS these three
1044	    /// bits (and the truth bits below them). Decomposed under v2 it is
1045	    /// `plast_bit2 | (w_slot << 1) | (truth << 7) | (band << 9)`. So a
1046	    /// non-zero band becomes the DOMINANT term of that composite.
1047	    ///
1048	    /// `Network::evidence_trail` sorts by `temporal()` and its comment claims
1049	    /// the sort "degrades to a stable no-op" under v2. That holds only while
1050	    /// bits 52..63 are all zero — it is already false for any edge carrying a
1051	    /// `w_slot` or a `truth`, and writing a band makes the ordering
1052	    /// band-dominated. That ordering is NOT meaningful. Nothing in-tree
1053	    /// writes a band today, so this is a trap for the first producer, not a
1054	    /// live defect.
1055	    /// the orthogonality notes, and the no-auto-derivation guarantee.
1056	    #[inline]
1057	    pub fn with_reasoning_band(self, band: crate::layout::ReasoningBand) -> Self {
1058	        use crate::layout::{BITS3_MASK, SPARE_MASK, SPARE_SHIFT};
