2	//!
3	//! The core insight: with 256 palette entries, there are only 65,536 possible
4	//! attention scores (256 × 256 pairs). Precompute them ALL. Every attention
5	//! score in every layer comes from the same 128KB table.
6	//!
7	//! ```text
8	//! Standard attention:           Q · K^T / √d     → O(d²) per pair
9	//! Palette attention:    table[q_idx][k_idx]        → O(1) per pair
10	//! ```
11	//!
12	//! The distance matrix gives you attention scores.
13	//! The compose table gives you multi-hop reasoning.
